### Register a Video Composition in src/Root.tsx

Source: https://github.com/remotion-dev/remotion/blob/main/packages/docs/docs/composition.mdx

Register a renderable video composition within the root component fragment to make it visible in the Remotion sidebar and ready for rendering.

```tsx
const Component: React.FC = () => null;
// ---cut---

import {Composition} from 'remotion';

export const RemotionRoot: React.FC = () => {
  return (
    <>
      <Composition component={Component} durationInFrames={300} width={1080} height={1080} fps={30} id="test-render" defaultProps={{}} />
      {/* Additional compositions can be rendered */}
    </>
  );
};
```

--------------------------------

### Create a deterministic fade-in with useCurrentFrame() and interpolate()

Source: https://github.com/remotion-dev/remotion/blob/main/packages/docs/docs/troubleshooting/css-animations.mdx

Derives animation values deterministically from the current frame using useCurrentFrame() and interpolate(). This ensures reproducible and frame-accurate rendering across all rendered frames.

```tsx
// ---cut---
import { AbsoluteFill, interpolate, useCurrentFrame } from "remotion";

export const FadeIn = () => {
  const frame = useCurrentFrame();
  const opacity = interpolate(frame, [0, 30], [0, 1], {
    extrapolateRight: "clamp",
  });

  return (
    <AbsoluteFill
      style={{
        justifyContent: "center",
        alignItems: "center",
        backgroundColor: "white",
        fontSize: 80,
      }}
    >
      <div style={{ opacity }}>Hello World!</div>
    </AbsoluteFill>
  );
};
```

--------------------------------

### <Still />

Source: https://github.com/remotion-dev/remotion/blob/main/packages/docs/docs/still.mdx

Defines a single-frame composition in Remotion for rendering images rather than video sequences. It shares the same properties as <Composition />, omitting durationInFrames and fps.

```APIDOC
## `<Still />`

### Description
A `<Still />` is a single-frame `<Composition />` component used to render static images instead of videos.

### Props
- **id** (string) - Required - Unique identifier for the composition.
- **component** (React.ComponentType) - Required - The React component to render as a still image.
- **width** (number) - Required - The width of the image in pixels.
- **height** (number) - Required - The height of the image in pixels.

### Usage Example
```tsx
import { Still } from 'remotion';
import { MyComp } from './MyComp';

export const RemotionRoot = () => {
  return (
    <Still
      id="my-image"
      component={MyComp}
      width={1080}
      height={1080}
    />
  );
};
```
```

--------------------------------

### Render a video with Remotion CLI

Source: https://github.com/remotion-dev/remotion/blob/main/packages/docs/docs/brownfield-installation.mdx

Renders a composition into a video file by specifying the entrypoint, composition ID, and output filename.

```bash
npx remotion render remotion/index.ts MyComp out.mp4
```

--------------------------------

### Render a still image with remotion still

Source: https://github.com/remotion-dev/remotion/blob/main/packages/codex-plugin/skills/remotion-best-practices/remotion-render/REFERENCE.md

Renders a single still frame using the Remotion CLI. Refer to the official Remotion CLI documentation for the full list of still options.

```bash
npx remotion still
```

